messages.content:
I'll inspect the actual project layout and the console/code-viewer components before answering.## 1. Short answer

There are three layers, and you always call the middle one:

```
ConsoleScriptConfirm.vue  (asks the user)   ← UI only
        ↓
$storex.api.console         ← what YOUR code calls
        ↓
POST /api/console/execute   ← ConsoleManager (scoping, timeout, capture)
```

From **any code** (Vue component or plain JS module):

```js
await API.console.runScript(script)                 // { name, script } or 'npm run dev'
await API.console.run('git status')                 // raw command
await API.console.execute({ command, cwd, env, timeout })   // full control
await API.console.info()                            // role, unrestricted, allowed_roots
```

The confirmation is **not** inside `runScript()` — it is a UI step you own. Below: how to wire it in each context.

---

## 2. Where the API instance comes from

| Context | How to get it |
|---|---|
| Options API component | `this.$storex.api` (what `ProjectScripts.vue` uses) |
| `<script setup>` | `const { proxy } = getCurrentInstance(); proxy.$storex.api` |
| Plain JS / Pinia / store file | `import { API } from '@/api/api'` |
| Console / devtools | `$storex.api` (global property) |

```js
// plain module, no component around
import { API } from '@/api/api'

const result = await API.console.run('npm run lint')
```

---

## 3. Executing from plain code — the three call styles

```js
// A. A project script (settings.project_scripts entry)
//    accepts the object or the raw string
const result = await API.console.runScript({ name: 'Dev', script: 'npm run dev' })

// B. A raw command, default cwd = project root
const result = await API.console.run('ls -la')

// C. Full control
const result = await API.console.execute({
  command: 'npm test',
  cwd: 'api',            // relative to the project, or absolute
  env: { NODE_ENV: 'test' },
  timeout: 120           // seconds, clamped to 1..300 (default 30)
})
```

`result` shape (same for all three):

```js
{
  command: 'npm test', cwd: '/path/to/project', user: 'gbrian',
  unrestricted: false, timeout: 120,
  stdout: '...', stderr: '...',
  exit_code: 0,        // null when it timed out
  timed_out: false
}
```

**HTTP 200 is not success** — always branch on `exit_code` / `timed_out`:

```js
const failed = result.timed_out || result.exit_code !== 0
```

Errors (`400` empty command / bad cwd / no project, `401`, `403` cwd outside your projects, `500` spawn failure) reject the promise:

```js
try {
  await API.console.run(cmd)
} catch (error) {
  const detail = error?.response?.data?.detail || error?.message
  proxy.$ui.addNotification({ text: detail, type: 'error' })
}
```

---

## 4. Executing a shell block coming from code / markdown

That is just case **B** — the command is a string, so no script object is needed:

```js
// a fenced ```bash block parsed by the chat/code viewer
const codeBlock = { language: 'bash', code: 'npm run build' }

if (['bash', 'sh', 'shell', 'zsh'].includes(codeBlock.language)) {
  const result = await API.console.run(codeBlock.code)
}
```

---

## 5. Executing from the CodeViewer component

Add a toolbar action that (1) asks for confirmation with the existing dialog, (2) calls `runScript`. Works the same whether the source of the command is `settings.project_scripts` or a code block.

```vue
<!-- src/components/repo/CodeViewer.vue (or any code panel) -->
<template>
  <div class="flex flex-col h-full">
    <!-- toolbar -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 p-2 border-b border-base-300">
      <span class="text-sm font-mono truncate grow">{{ fileName }}</span>

      <button
        class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost"
        :disabled="!runnableScript"
        :title="runnableScript ? 'Run this script in the console' : 'No script to run'"
        aria-label="Run script in the console"
        @click="requestRun(runnableScript)"
      >
        <i class="fa-solid fa-terminal"></i>
      </button>
    </div>

    <!-- editor / viewer -->
    <div class="grow overflow-auto"><pre class="text-xs">{{ content }}</pre></div>

    <!-- confirmation -->
    <ConsoleScriptConfirm
      :show="!!scriptToRun"
      :script="scriptToRun"
      :busy="running"
      @confirm="confirmRun"
      @cancel="scriptToRun = null"
    />
  </div>
</template>

<script setup>
import { computed, getCurrentInstance, ref } from 'vue'
import ConsoleScriptConfirm from '@/components/console/ConsoleScriptConfirm.vue'

const props = defineProps({
  fileName: { type: String, default: '' },
  content: { type: String, default: '' },
  // optional: a script object ({ name, script }) or a raw command string
  script: { type: [Object, String], default: null },
  // directory used as cwd, relative to the project root
  cwd: { type: String, default: null }
})

const { proxy } = getCurrentInstance()

const scriptToRun = ref(null)
const running = ref(false)
const lastRun = ref(null)

// Normalize whatever we got into something ConsoleScriptConfirm can render
const runnableScript = computed(() => {
  if (!props.script) return null
  return typeof props.script === 'string'
    ? { name: props.fileName || 'Command', script: props.script }
    : props.script
})

function requestRun(script) {
  if (!script) return
  scriptToRun.value = script          // dialog opens here, nothing executed yet
}

async function confirmRun() {
  if (!scriptToRun.value || running.value) return
  running.value = true
  try {
    lastRun.value = await proxy.$storex.api.console.runScript(
      scriptToRun.value,
      props.cwd ? { cwd: props.cwd } : undefined
    )
    scriptToRun.value = null
  } catch (error) {
    proxy.$ui.addNotification({
      text: error?.response?.data?.detail || error?.message,
      type: 'error'
    })
  } finally {
    running.value = false
  }
}
</script>
```

Options-API variant (same logic, matching `ProjectScripts.vue` style):

```js
export default {
  data: () => ({ scriptToRun: null, running: false, lastRun: null }),
  methods: {
    requestRun(script) { if (script) this.scriptToRun = script },
    async confirmRun() {
      this.running = true
      try {
        this.lastRun = await this.$storex.api.console.runScript(this.scriptToRun)
        this.scriptToRun = null
      } catch (error) {
        this.$ui.addNotification({ text: error?.response?.data?.detail || error?.message, type: 'error' })
      } finally {
        this.running = false
      }
    }
  }
}
```

---

## 6. Optional: one composable instead of copy-pasting

If several components need it (`CodeViewer`, `ProjectScripts`, chat code blocks), extract the confirm/run/notify cycle:

```js
// src/composables/useConsole.js
import { getCurrentInstance, ref } from 'vue'
import { consoleScriptCommand } from '@/api/modules/console'

export function useConsole() {
  const { proxy } = getCurrentInstance()
  const api = proxy.$storex.api

  const scriptToRun = ref(null)
  const running = ref(false)
  const lastRun = ref(null)

  const failed = () => lastRun.value?.timed_out || lastRun.value?.exit_code !== 0

  function requestRun(script, options = {}) {
    const command = consoleScriptCommand(script)
    if (!command) return false
    scriptToRun.value = { ...(typeof script === 'object' ? script : {}), script: command, ...options }
    return true
  }

  function cancelRun() { if (!running.value) scriptToRun.value = null }

  async function confirmRun() {
    const target = scriptToRun.value
    if (!target || running.value) return null
    running.value = true
    try {
      const { name, description, background, restart, ...options } = target
      lastRun.value = await api.console.runScript(target, options)
      return lastRun.value
    } catch (error) {
      proxy.$ui.addNotification({
        text: error?.response?.data?.detail || error?.message,
        type: 'error'
      })
      return null
    } finally {
      running.value = false
      scriptToRun.value = null
    }
  }

  // direct execution, no dialog (only when the caller already asked)
  const run = (command, options) => api.console.run(command, options)
  const info = () => api.console.info()

  return { scriptToRun, running, lastRun, failed, requestRun, cancelRun, confirmRun, run, info }
}
```

Usage becomes 3 lines in any component:

```vue
<script setup>
const { scriptToRun, running, requestRun, confirmRun, cancelRun } = useConsole()
</script>
```

---

## 7. Rules that bite

| Rule | Consequence |
|---|---|
| `runScript` executes **immediately** | Never bind it to a bare click; go through `requestRun` + dialog |
| Confirmation needs the **command text**, not just the name | `ConsoleScriptConfirm` renders `script.script`; pass the normalized object |
| `cwd` is validated server-side | Non-admins get `403` outside their projects — surface `detail`, don't silently swallow |
| Timeout default **30 s**, max **300 s** | Long tasks die with `timed_out: true` and `exit_code: null` |
| `background: true` **is not honoured** | `subprocess.run` waits; a dev server runs until the timeout. Don't offer "Run" for those from the CodeViewer |
| `exit_code !== 0` is a normal `200` | Never infer success from the absence of a rejection |
| Admin users are unrestricted | `info().unrestricted` tells you if you may pass an absolute `cwd` |

